description.p:
Another object of the invention is to realize an automated device that, while utilizing a conventional milking unit, is very effective and reliable in the practice and also able, because of its structural simplicity, to allow the direct intervention by the operator, if any breakdowns and/or functional anomalies should occur. 

These and still other objects, that will be better stressed later on, are achieved by a mechanical device for the positioning and the attachment, in an automated manner, of the nipple-graspers to the nipples of a milk cow in a milking station slave to a robot of a known type, comprising known sensing means, suitably located in the space surrounding the milk cow, for the identification of the position of the individual nipples and the sending of the signals they emit to said robot intended for positioning said nipple-graspers along the vertical of said nipples, which device comprises, according to the present invention: a milking unit constituted of four nipple- graspers, connected through usual short milk and vacuum tubes to an underlying collector, which is kept hanging and in a vertically translatable manner through at least a flexible element, to a supporting element connected to said robot, in order to allow said collector to oscillate freely in all directions; positioning means for each of said nipple- graspers, constituted of arched seats, substantially niches, obtained at the free end of said supporting element connected to the robot, said seats being so arranged as to keep each nipple-grasper in a well defined position, to allow 

afterwards the sequential attachment to the related nipple by the movement of said supporting element;
